app mock-page-seed-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for per-page mock seeding: a route mount delivers $MOUNT { page, route, traits, entities } (EXEC-SEED-7) to the MockSeed trait of std-mock-page-seed, which reads the running program with program/self and seeds the page's entities that mock_seed_marks does not yet name, then marks them. An empty entity list seeds nothing; a revisit seeds nothing; another page seeds only its own unseeded entities. The same machine serves orb serve (composed into the served app) and the catalog (composed into the guest program). The replay cases live with std-mock-seed (spec/dev/mock-seed-input.replay.goldens.json, the seed-page-* cases) and the composition is checked by spec/dev/mock-page-seed.replay.goldens.json."
]
